  <items>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp115753448">mineadh</headword>
      <description>Quotation: Mineadh [mĩṉəɡ] ort! Notes: used in the same way as “m’ullaidh ort!”</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp115749992">sgrios</headword>
      <description>Quotation: Sgrios obainn gu robh ort! Notes: heard one tinker wife say this to another when chiding her for drinking all the milk they had just got.</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp115746680">toirsgean</headword>
      <description>[t̪ɔʴsɡʹəṉ] Notes: peat-cutting iron. [NOTES: the turned r used for the symbol which is unclear in the original.]</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <headword id="idp115766408">am feasda</headword>
      <description>Quotation: Chan fhaic mi e a feasda. Notes: I’ll never see him.</description>
    </item>
